1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
Most road-trip breakdowns

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:03,000
start as a ten-minute check
somebody skipped.

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,500
Four: tread depth.

4
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:08,000
Worn tread on hot highway miles
is a blowout waiting on a schedule.

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,500
Three: pressure — all five tires,

6
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:13,000
including the spare nobody's
checked since it came off the truck.

7
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,500
Two: belts and hoses.

8
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:18,000
A hairline crack you can't feel
is exactly what quits at mile 200.

9
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,500
One: fluid levels.

10
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:23,000
Low is cheap in the driveway.
Empty is expensive on the shoulder.

11
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,500
All four, one visit,
before you go.

12
